This repo's rules live in three files. Read them before writing code; don't duplicate them here.

- @CLAUDE.md: always-on rules, the design-system change policy, the Figma-variable → Tailwind class table, commands and known limits.
- @.claude/skills/figma-to-prototype/SKILL.md: the step-by-step workflow for any request that includes a Figma URL (read the design, map components and gaps, fix the design system, build, verify).
- @../linarc-design-components/PRPs/prototype-changes/README.md: how to change the library, and the change log.

Key points if you read nothing else:
- Vue 2.7 Options API, plain JS. No Composition API or `<script setup>`. No TypeScript.
- Use `@/componentsV2/*`, then `@/components/*`. No hand-built lookalikes. If the library is wrong or missing something, fix it, fork it or add it, and flag and log every change.
- Token classes only (`bg-surface-*`, `text-text-*`, `p-space-N`, `rounded-radius-N`). No hex, raw or arbitrary values.
- Responsive from 390px to 1440px+.
- Verify at 1440, 1024 and 390px wide, in light and dark, with `yarn shot <slug>` before reporting done.
- Record every prototype and finding in `docs/` (skill step 6; see `docs/README.md`).
